From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:40:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/31] Finder AirDrop: transfer progress cards, Share >
 AirDrop sheet with Wi-Fi warning, notifications

FinderAirDrop (one per process) runs omdrop: discovery, peers and sends.
Send progress comes from how far the sending processes have read each file
(/proc/PID/fdinfo); incoming transfers are followed in the receiver's log
and sized from the file it is writing. Cards in the window's corner show
both; finished sends raise a system notification. Share > AirDrop in the
context menu (and AirDrop... in the actions menu) opens a sheet over the
current folder: Wi-Fi warning, then nearby devices; AirDrop is switched
off again afterwards if the sheet switched it on.

